From fc901897d5999e69da8084c2aaf2f88ac8d82525
Subject: bevy_animation: replace evaluator hashmaps with dense index lists
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/fc901897d5999e69da8084c2aaf2f88ac8d82525
Date: 2026-07-06T19:42:47+01:00

AnimationCurveEvaluators and CurrentEvaluators were probed per curve
per target per frame (PreHashMap + TypeIdMap probes in
get_or_insert_with, push_blend_register_all, and the commit_all
drain). The distinct-evaluator count is bounded by the number of
animatable properties (translation/rotation/scale/weights in
glTF-driven content), not scene size, so a linear scan over a dense
Vec beats hashing, and the current-evaluator set reduces to a Vec of
indices into it: the per-graph-node blend/add/push/commit loops become
direct array indexing with no key comparisons. Collections live in the
retained thread-local state, so capacity is allocated once per thread.

Genesis Plaza (wasm, 8 shadow casters): animation group 7.55% -> 5.03%
of frame; the evaluator-map probe, CurrentEvaluators::clear, and
push_blend_register_all profile entries disappear entirely.

Also picks up a missed rustfmt in graph.rs from an earlier commit.
